<BaseLayout title="About Gennaro Basile" description="From mechanical engineering and automotive validation to Data Science, AI engineering and community building.">
  <header class="shell py-20"><p class="eyebrow text-orange">About / Gennaro Basile</p><h1 class="display mt-8">A path that<br />doesn’t fit in<br /><em class="font-serif font-normal text-orange">one discipline.</em></h1></header>
  <section class="shell grid gap-12 pb-24 lg:grid-cols-[.55fr_1fr]"><aside class="border-l-4 border-purple pl-6"><p class="eyebrow">Now</p><p class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Data Science master’s student at the University of Naples Federico II, building toward AI Engineering.</p></aside><article class="prose"><p>My path has never fitted neatly inside one discipline. I started in mechanical engineering and spent several years working in automotive validation between Italy and Michigan. The work taught me how physical systems fail, how evidence changes decisions, and why details matter.</p><p>I chose to return to Naples and make learning central to my work again. I enrolled in the Data Science master’s programme at the University of Naples Federico II to build stronger foundations in statistics, machine learning and software—not as a nostalgic return, but as an active decision about what I want to build next.</p><p>I have always been multipotential: drawn to engineering, research, visual communication, communities and the process of turning ideas into real things. AI gives me a way to connect these interests instead of forcing them apart.</p><h2>Buildspace081</h2><p>The same desire to learn through other people led me to create <a href="https://buildspace081.com/">Buildspace081</a>: a community for people who want to build real things together in Naples, and a local environment where founders, engineers and curious people can meet.</p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
